---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro';
const command = `curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -fsSL https://ouroboros.monocursive.com/install.sh | bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"
ouro-jail doctor --profile tool`;
const capabilities = [
  { title: 'File access', text: 'Give the process a workspace and specific read-only or writable paths. Your home directory is not exposed by default. System runtime files remain available so programs can execute.' },
  { title: 'Network access', text: 'Local tools and builds run without a network. Agents connect through a proxy that checks destinations against your allowlist. You choose which services they can reach.' },
  { title: 'Runtime limits', text: 'Set a deadline for the command. Add memory, CPU, and process limits on hosts with delegated cgroup controls. If a required control is unavailable, the jail refuses the run.' },
  { title: 'A record of the run', text: 'A receipt records the policy that was applied, the result, and any missing evidence. Observation is on by default and logs a defined set of operations; it does not capture every action.' },
];
const useCases = [
  { profile: 'agent', title: 'Let a coding agent work on a project', text: 'Make the checkout writable and allow the model endpoints it needs. Keep unrelated projects and credentials outside its file grants. Review the diff when it finishes.' },
  { profile: 'tool', title: 'Run tests from an unfamiliar repository', text: 'Use a disposable checkout with no network access and a time limit. Grant installed dependencies as read-only paths when needed.' },
  { profile: 'build', title: 'Build from read-only source', text: 'Give a build command read-only inputs, a writable output directory, and scratch space. Set a memory limit and keep the network closed.' },
];
const upcoming = [
  { status: 'Next', title: 'Broader host compatibility', text: 'Extend clean-machine installation and enforcement records beyond the reference Linux hosts.' },
  { status: 'Next', title: 'More tested agents', text: 'Run each agent and version against a current jail build, then publish the compatibility results and updated benchmarks.' },
  { status: 'Research', title: 'Native macOS execution', text: 'Resolve process cleanup when the supervising helper dies. Apple entitlement approval is also pending; approval alone will not make execution ready.' },
];
const benchmark = 'https://github.com/monocursive/ouroboros/blob/dev/docs/benchmarks/jail/followup-2026-09-29.md#k17-results';
---
<Site title="Ouroboros Jail — A Linux sandbox for AI agents" description="Give your AI agent only the access it needs. Restrict files, network destinations, and runtime, with receipts and recorded Linux benchmarks.">
  <section class="hero container" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow status"><span class="status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> Developer preview 0.1.0-rc.1 · Linux x86_64 + ARM64</p>
      <h1 id="hero-heading">Give your agent only the access it needs.</h1>
      <p class="introduction">Ouroboros Jail is a Linux sandbox for AI agents and command-line tools. Limit which files they can change, which services they can contact, and how long they can run.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="/guide/">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#security">How it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
    </div>
    <div class="emblem" aria-hidden="true">
      <img class="orbit orbit-outer" src="/brand/orbit-outer.svg" width="440" height="440" alt="" />
      <img class="orbit orbit-middle" src="/brand/orbit-middle.svg" width="346" height="346" alt="" />
      <img class="orbit orbit-inner" src="/brand/orbit-inner.svg" width="242" height="242" alt="" />
      <img class="hero-mark" src="/brand/ouroboros.svg" width="380" height="380" alt="" fetchpriority="high" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container example" aria-labelledby="example-heading">
    <div class="terminal">
      <div class="terminal-heading"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="example-heading">Install the developer preview</h2><span class="eyebrow">Signed Linux packages</span></div>
      <pre tabindex="0"><code>{command}</code></pre>
    </div>
    <div class="example-notes"><p>Requires glibc 2.39+ and bubblewrap. SHA-256 hashes are pinned in the installer. Installs to ~/.local/bin without Minisign or a Rust compiler. Use doctor to check your host.</p><a href="/guide/#install-the-developer-preview">Install &amp; host requirements ↗</a></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="security" aria-labelledby="security-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow section-eyebrow">Security</p>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="security-heading">Enforce permissions outside the agent.</h2><p>The <code>ouro-jail</code> command uses bubblewrap and Linux kernel controls to restrict a process and its children. Your existing agent keeps its own models and workflow.</p></div>
      <div class="capabilities">{capabilities.map((item) => <article class="capability"><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div>
      <div class="workflow-note"><h3>The grants still matter.</h3><p>An agent can change files you make writable and send readable data to services you allow. Start with a small set of permissions and inspect the result. Containment relies on the host kernel; this is pre-release software with security review still ahead of release.</p><a class="text-link" href="/guide/#understand-the-boundary">Understand the boundary <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="use-cases" aria-labelledby="use-cases-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow section-eyebrow">Use cases</p>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="use-cases-heading">Where the jail helps</h2><p>Pick a profile for the job, then grant the paths and services that command needs.</p></div>
      <div class="use-case-grid">{useCases.map((item) => <article><p class="eyebrow">{item.profile} profile</p><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div>
      <a class="text-link section-link" href="/guide/#choose-a-profile">Choose a profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="performance" aria-labelledby="performance-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow section-eyebrow">Performance</p>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="performance-heading">What does the sandbox cost?</h2><p>Processes run on the host kernel. Setting up containment takes time, and observing operations adds work while the command runs.</p></div>
      <div class="performance-grid">
        <div class="performance-copy">
          <p>In our recorded Linux benchmark, the highest p95 added startup time across the tested workloads was <strong>131 ms with observation off</strong>.</p>
          <p><strong>Observation is on by default.</strong> In the file-heavy fixture shown here, it raised median total runtime from 375 ms to 1,167 ms. Expect the cost to depend on what your command does.</p>
          <p class="measurement-note">Recorded on 29 September 2026 on the Ubuntu reference host, using an earlier development build. These are synthetic workloads, not an agent speed estimate.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="benchmark-table">
          <table>
            <caption>5,000 file-operation rounds<br /><span>Median total runtime · plain session · 30 samples per mode</span></caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Execution mode</th><th scope="col">Time</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Direct, without the jail</th><td>190 ms</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Jailed, observation off</th><td>375 ms</td></tr>
              <tr class="default-mode"><th scope="row">Jailed, observation on <span>Default</span></th><td>1,167 ms</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="benchmark-note">The full benchmark contains 540 measured launches. All 60 observation-off no-op runs finished too quickly for the jail to confirm execution and returned <code>exec_unconfirmed</code> with exit code 1. Their startup timings are included; they are not successful run receipts.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href={benchmark}>Read the method, raw results, and limitations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="status-heading">
    <div class="container status-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow section-eyebrow">Availability</p><h2 id="status-heading">Start on Linux.</h2></div>
      <div class="status-copy">
        <p><strong>Signed developer packages are available for Linux x86_64 and ARM64.</strong> Read the <a href="https://github.com/monocursive/ouroboros/releases/tag/ouro-jail-v0.1.0-rc.1">release notes</a> and use <code>doctor</code> to check your host. macOS builds can inspect policy, but currently refuse sandboxed execution.</p>
        <p>Fourteen starter launch profiles are included. OpenCode has recorded live runs; other agent and version combinations still need testing.</p>
        <p>When a command needs more access, <code>learn</code> can propose missing read and network permissions from an observed run. You review the proposal before applying it.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/guide/#run-an-existing-agent">Run an existing agent <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="next-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow section-eyebrow">Planned work</p>
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="next-heading">What we’re working on next</h2><a class="text-link" href="/roadmap/">Read the roadmap <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div class="roadmap-grid">{upcoming.map((item) => <article><p class="eyebrow">{item.status}</p><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div>
      <p class="later-note">Shared run records and company-managed Linux workers are planned further out. There are no release dates for these yet.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
